      <title>intel userspace</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>X.org+OpenICC Devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Updates from the Intel userland: GL, X, and infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Much has changed for the better in Linux graphics in the last few years. The radical changes driver architecture to make compositing possible are&#xA;stabilized and mainstream, new desktop environments are popping up regularly making use of these features, and OpenGL is changing from a usually buggy luxury component to a standard working part of Linux.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this talk, Eric will cover what has been going on in the Intel graphics driver stack to stabilize Linux graphics and catch up to the&#xA;capabilities of of the hardware.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description></description>
      <persons>
          <person id="1591">Eric Anholt</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>